{"group":"gulf_littoral","label":"Gulf","note":"The eight states on the Gulf. A geographic group, not an organisation: it is not the GCC and not OPEC.","statement":"National energy statistics for the 8 Gulf systems, for context. A figure here is a country's annual total. It says nothing about any facility, and it is never used to weigh, rank or score a disruption.","not_built":"This view has no route, strait, shipping or tanker information, no facility layer and no measure of dependence or importance, by design.","memberships":{"gcc":{"label":"GCC","note":"Members of the Gulf Cooperation Council. Iran and Iraq are not members.","members":["bh","kw","om","qa","sa","ae"]},"opec":{"label":"OPEC","note":"Monitored systems that are OPEC members today. The United Arab Emirates left on 2026-05-01, as its government announced on 2026-04-28; OPEC's own member page refused access when this was checked, so the list rests on that announcement as reported. Membership is context only; an OPEC production decision is policy, never a disruption record.","members":["ir","iq","kw","sa"]}},"order":"alphabetical by name; never by any figure","sources":{"eia-international-energy-statistics":{"name":"U.S. Energy Information Administration, International Energy Statistics","url":"https://www.eia.gov/international/data/world","release":"2026-10-16","attribution":"Source: U.S. Energy Information Administration, International Energy Statistics."}},"metrics":{"total_production":{"label":"Total primary energy production","unit":"quadrillion Btu","source_series":"INTL.44-1","source_unit_tag":"QBTU","definition":"EIA total energy production: coal, natural gas, petroleum and other liquids, nuclear, and renewables and other, in one energy unit.","year":2024,"source_id":"eia-international-energy-statistics"},"crude_production":{"label":"Crude oil production","unit":"thousand barrels per day","source_series":"INTL.57-1","source_unit_tag":"TBPD","definition":"EIA crude oil including lease condensate."